# State & Event Architecture

Rules for managing game state and socket/DOM event flow. Based on scattered state, dual-listener conflicts, and race conditions found in this project.

---

## Centralized Game State

Game state must live in a **single, typed state object** per game session — not scattered across screen fields, phase fields, and module-level variables.

### Anti-Pattern — Scattered State (DO NOT)

```ts
// BAD: State is everywhere
// In GameScreen.ts:
public gameState: GAME_STATE = GAME_STATE.SHUFFLING_CARDS;
public allowedAction: ALLOW_ACTIONS[] | null = null;
private isOpponentTakenTurn: boolean = false;
private isFirstTurn: boolean = true;

// In eventListeners.ts (module-level):
let currentGameUserId: string | null = null;
let currentRound: number = 1;
let lastColumnResultHadDealerBust: boolean = false;

// In TurnInfoManage singleton:
private earlyTurnInfo: TurnInfo | null = null;
```

### Correct Pattern — State Manager

```ts
// GOOD: Single source of truth
class GameSessionState {
  readonly gameUserId: string;
  readonly matchId: string;
  gameState: GAME_STATE = GAME_STATE.IDLE;
  allowedActions: ALLOW_ACTIONS[] = [];
  currentRound = 1;
  isOpponentTakenTurn = false;
  isFirstTurn = true;
  lastColumnResultHadDealerBust = false;
  pendingTurnInfo: TurnInfo | null = null;

  constructor(init: { gameUserId: string; matchId: string }) {
    this.gameUserId = init.gameUserId;
    this.matchId = init.matchId;
  }

  reset() {
    this.gameState = GAME_STATE.IDLE;
    this.allowedActions = [];
    this.currentRound = 1;
    this.isOpponentTakenTurn = false;
    this.isFirstTurn = true;
    this.lastColumnResultHadDealerBust = false;
    this.pendingTurnInfo = null;
  }
}
```

### Rules
- One `GameSessionState` instance per active game. Created when a game starts, passed to screens and phases by reference.
- Screens and phases read/write the shared state object — they do not maintain private copies.
- Module-level `let` variables for game state are forbidden. Use the state object.

