## Typed Socket Events

Socket event names and payloads must have compile-time type safety. No `string + unknown` signatures.

### Define an Event Map

```ts
// types/socketEvents.ts
export interface ServerToClientEvents {
  [EVENTS.TURN_INFO]: (data: TurnInfoPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.SETUP_DONE]: (data: SetupDonePayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.COLUMN_UPDATE]: (data: ColumnUpdatePayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.GAME_TABLE_INFO]: (data: GameTableInfoPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.SHUFFLE_DECK]: (data: ShuffleDeckPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.ROUND_STARTING]: (data: RoundStartingPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.GAME_RESULT_SCREEN]: (data: GameResultPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.WAITING_FOR_OPPONENT]: (data: WaitingPayload) => void;
}

export interface ClientToServerEvents {
  [EVENTS.JOIN_GAME]: (data: JoinGamePayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.PLAYER_ACTION]: (data: PlayerActionPayload) => void;
  [EVENTS.LEAVE_GAME]: (data: LeaveGamePayload) => void;
}
```

### Typed Socket Interface

```ts
export interface ISocketManager {
  on<K extends keyof ServerToClientEvents>(
    event: K,
    callback: ServerToClientEvents[K]
  ): void;

  off<K extends keyof ServerToClientEvents>(
    event: K,
    callback: ServerToClientEvents[K]
  ): void;

  emit<K extends keyof ClientToServerEvents>(
    event: K,
    ...args: Parameters<ClientToServerEvents[K]>
  ): void;
}
```

### Rules
- Every socket event must have a corresponding payload type in `types/socketEvents.ts`.
- The `ISocketManager` interface must use the event map for type-safe `on`/`off`/`emit`.
- When the server adds a new event, add its type to the map FIRST, then implement handlers.
- Event constant names (`EVENTS.TURN_INFO`) must match the event map keys exactly.

