## Navigation Contract

The `Navigation` class must ONLY handle screen transitions. It must not:

- Fetch data from APIs
- Map currencies
- Transform wallet data
- Execute partner-specific logic

### Current Violation

```ts
// BAD — Navigation.goBackToLobby does data fetching and currency mapping
async goBackToLobby() {
  const walletData = await apiClient.getWallet();
  const mapped = walletData.currencies.map(c => {
    if (c.currencyCode === "EMT") c.currencyCode = CURRENCY_CODES.PLAY_COINS;
    // ...
  });
  this.showScreen(LobbyScreen, { walletData: mapped });
}
```

### Correct Pattern

```ts
// GOOD — Dedicated service for data, Navigation only transitions
class WalletService {
  async getWalletForLobby(): Promise<MappedWalletData> {
    const raw = await this.apiClient.getWallet();
    return this.mapCurrencies(raw);
  }
}

// Navigation just shows screens
async goBackToLobby() {
  const walletData = await walletService.getWalletForLobby();
  this.showScreen(LobbyScreen, { walletData });
}
```

### Rules
- Navigation may accept data as a parameter and pass it to the screen constructor.
- Navigation must not import or use `apiClient`, `socketManager`, or partner-specific constants.
- Data preparation (API calls, transformations) belongs in dedicated service classes that are called BEFORE invoking navigation.

