## DOM Event Management

### Rules for `window` Events

- Track all `window.addEventListener` calls and their handler references.
- Remove all listeners when the owning screen is hidden/destroyed.
- Events like `visibilitychange`, `resize`, `message`, and `appMessage` must follow the same stored-reference pattern described in `pixijs-oop-patterns.mdc`.

### Global vs Screen-Scoped DOM Events

| Event | Scope | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| `resize` | Global (app lifetime) | `app.ts` — register once at startup |
| `visibilitychange` | Global | `app.ts` or dedicated `VisibilityManager` |
| `message` / `appMessage` | Screen-scoped | Active screen — register in `show()`, remove in `hide()` |
| `keydown` / `input` | Screen-scoped | Active screen or `InputManager` |
| `error` / `unhandledrejection` | Global | `sentry.ts` — register once at startup |

Global listeners registered at app startup are acceptable since they live for the app's lifetime. Screen-scoped listeners MUST be cleaned up on screen transitions.
